"""The scanner's training data generator (docs/scan-training.md → "Kept apart", "Made-up sets: build, verify, QA"):
`python -m gen <command>`. Torch-free and Google-free, so the tests in CI import it. The split rule and the class
table (gen/common.py), the sources registry (gen/sources.py: `sources`), the random streams (gen/rng.py), the manifest,
run.json and the data fingerprint (gen/manifest.py), today's generators through the manifest (gen/build.py: `build`),
drawing a sample again (gen/verify.py: `verify`), the QA sheet (gen/qa.py: `qa`), the scenes — flat pages with field boxes (gen/pages.py), one camera for the table and the documents (gen/camera.py, gen/scene.py), the edges models' writer (gen/outputs/edges.py: `build --model edges`) — and the background bank (gen/backgrounds.py: `bg`, `occluders`), the phone's input path (gen/phone.py, its kernels in gen/phone_profile.json: `profile`) the edges exam on it (gen/exam_phone.py: `exam-phone`) the phone's own cuts (gen/phone_run.py with the writers gen/outputs/doctype.py, mrz.py, he.py, face.py: `build --model doctype,mrz,he,face`), the real data labelled only from what a person did (gen/real.py: `real`), one training list per model with the real data repeated (gen/mix.py: `mix`) and the QA sheet's realism panel (gen/qa.py)."""
